  <reporting-org ref="GB-GOV-1" type="10">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UK - Foreign, Commonwealth Development Office (FCDO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Evaluation of CDC&apos;s Capital Increase - Multi-sector Evaluation of the Development Impact of CDC&#x2019;s Investments: Health; Education</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The evaluation is one of a series of sectoral evaluations being undertaken across British International Investment&apos;s (BII) portfolio to assess BII&#x2019;s overall performance and effectiveness. The purpose of this evaluation is to better understand the development outcomes and impacts associated with BII&#x2019;s investments in Services (including health, education, consumer and business services); manufacturing; agriculture; real estate; &amp; technology sectors (&#x2018;SMART Industries&#x2019; and draw out key learnings. Key components include: An in-depth portfolio evaluation of BII&#x2019;s investments in the five SMART sectors; A series of ten in-depth studies addressing targeted research and evaluation questions relevant to BII and/or its investees in these sectors; and, A final assessment drawing together key learning and understanding of impact from all stages of the evaluation. Study renamed &apos; Industries, Technology and Services (ITS)&apos; instead of &apos;SMART&apos;.</narrative>
  </description>
